  "deviations": [
    "State reached through the real flow: the sealed copy is put on the device behind a PIN (mocked download, sealed here with the same AES-GCM format), then the witness box opens it with the PIN. The page is the offline route; nothing but the copy's status check is asked.",
    "The bar says 'Trial'; the board says 'Mrs A · Trial'. The sealed copy carries no case name (patient data is not kept on the device), so the artboard is rendered with 'Trial' too (artboardCss).",
    "Gap: the copy's facts carry a fact kind, not a source type, so the chip shows the kind's words in the one green style; the board colours the second entry's edge and chip blue (the pack's hospital source colour). The artboard is rendered in green for comparison. Also not in the copy (format v1): the clinician and setting ('Dr P · face to face'), and which report paragraph cites the entry ('In your report at para 5.13'); the page prints the date alone and no paragraph for a fact.",
    "The search highlights the words typed ('15 May'); the board highlights 'PR bleeding x3/52' in the first entry, which the artboard has switched off for comparison.",
    "Exit keeps a 52px hit area (the board draws it 46px tall); the bar stays 72px tall.",
    "Body and small text under 17px is 17px (chip, count, footer), as in every screen."
  ]
